{
  "_about": "Learning topics: one subject that cuts across tracks (version control, accessibility, runbooks...). Each topic lists where its questions come from, as `track` (all of it) or `track:group,group` (named card groups of that track, see content/cards). scripts/build-topic-tracks.ts copies those questions into one track per topic ('topic-<slug>') so the topic can be required, raced and certified like any other track. Only generic content may be a source: a shared-academy track (minus its groups about one company), or what `genericTracks` lists from a company track (`*` = all of it, or just the named groups). Company-specific tracks (Moksy, GGLink, Guru Graphics...) never feed a topic that every company can see. A topic with no sources is a known gap: it is reported and no track is made.",
